{title: O My Strength}
{subtitle: Psalms 59:16–17}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 73}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] | [F/A] | [Gm7] | [Eb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
They return at eve[Bb]ning, s[F/A]narling like [Gm7]dogs
[Eb]Prowling around the city in the [Fsus4]dark
[F]They roam about for [Bb]food, [F/A]un[Gm7]satisfied
And [Eb]howl through the night without a [Fsus4]rest
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
[F]For [Gm]the sin of their mouths, let them be [Dm]caught
In their own [Eb]pride, by the lies they [Fsus4]tell
[F]Con[Gm]sume them in wrath until they [Dm]are gone
Then they [Eb]will know God rules over Ja[Fsus4]cob
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[F]But I will [Bb]sing [F/A]of your [Gm]strength
In [Eb]the morning I [Bb/D]will [F]sing aloud of your mercy
[Bb]You have [F/A]been my [Gm]fortress
My [Eb]refuge in the day [F]of my dis[Bb]tress
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
To the [Bbmaj7/A]ends of the [Bb]earth your [F/A]rule is [Gm]known
[Eb]The proud are consumed in your holy [F]wrath
The [Bb]snarling dogs circle and [F/A]find [Gm]no food
[Eb]Their howling fades into the [F]silence
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
But I will [Bb]sing [F/A]of your [Gm]strength
In [Eb]the morning I [Bb/D]will sing [F]aloud of your mercy
[Bb]You have [F/A]been my [Gm]fortress
My [Eb]refuge in the day [F]of my dis[Bb]tress
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Eb]O [F]my [Gm]Strength, [Eb]to [F]you I [Gm]sing praise
For [Eb]God [F]is my [Gm]fortress
[Eb][F]My God of mer[Bb]cy
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
But I will sing [F/A]of your [Gm]strength
In the [Eb]morning I will [Bb/D]sing a[F]loud of your mercy
Savior, [Bb]you have [F/A]been my [Gm]fortress
My [Eb]refuge in the day [F]of my dis[Gm]tress [Eb]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[F]My God of mer[Bb]cy [Eb]
[F]O my [Bb]Strength
{end_of_verse}
